eratorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{4+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{4+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{4\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}.$ \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{4+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c1681a73dd1fc724fb66e2e506c6e6119ccfd747f9f76c781b5a661e273fcbd" "basis" 1259 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-49505" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037171/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "31e77975055356d