249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3\\,\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}=3\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $6x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}3\\int \\frac{1}{|6x|\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(36x)}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{36}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(36x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-73715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{8}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{8}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-114056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})+C"] ["math" "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/16)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{4}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19393" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡($\n{{field-1}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/12)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/12}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{12})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{12}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{12}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{12})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}{\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-351855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\, & ={\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/25)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/25}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-114074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-114074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can write this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $25{x}^{2}=(5x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{20}{3+75{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/5}\\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4207968f4e09770be703843106668d261c81eac2351ac6724a5e99fb8a907a0b"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "q-19396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/state.json" "file_sha256" "209bc00cb40175a9943a64f62fd3f5191b12be9d808b34cf249d94d8af200e70"} {"question" "e-470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9x^2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-470.json" "file_sha256" "1435394612aecb48eb059230fa8b1c3c746e91a96bae660cc7ef755955f4e4c4"} {"question" "e-470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-u^2}}\\textrm{d}u = \\arcsin(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $9x^2 = (3x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 3 \\,\\textrm d u=\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{4\\sqrt{1-9{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x)^{2}}}\\,\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-470.json" "file_sha256" "1435394612aecb48eb059230fa8b1c3c746e91a96bae660cc7ef755955f4e4c4"} {"question" "e-471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral  $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-471.json" "file_sha256" "a975caa500c4657b7f477c9ceb80ab5761d91a2717f5f9ceac15f087b25261ec"} {"question" "e-471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{3}{2 + 50x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int \\dfrac{3}{2(1 + 25x^2)} = \\dfrac 3 2 \\int \\dfrac{1}{1+25x^2}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^2}\\textrm{d}u =\\arctan u +C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u^2$ as the variable, we have $25x^2 = (5x)^2.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac 1 5\\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2+50{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+25{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(5x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡5x+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-471.json" "file_sha256" "a975caa500c4657b7f477c9ceb80ab5761d91a2717f5f9ceac15f087b25261ec"} {"question" "e-5014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5\\, \\textrm{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^2-1}}  = }$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-5014.json" "file_sha256" "35f9523f03b71884abfc10e15c0a26d9f10bcb0587c6a3ed222655da25b76ee8"} {"question" "e-5014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This resembles the basic integral for $\\textrm{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^2-1}} \\textrm{d}u = \\textrm{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nLet $u = 5x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=5\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n5\\,\\textrm{d}x = \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5\\,\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}} & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(u)+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-5014.json" "file_sha256" "35f9523f03b71884abfc10e15c0a26d9f10bcb0587c6a3ed222655da25b76ee8"} {"question" "e-472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt 2} \\dfrac{1}{2+x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-472.json" "file_sha256" "6971fcf80e5ddd49db1502806ec3e5d5058537acead60eadae43d95f96e66011"} {"question" "e-472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+{x}^{2}/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2(1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this integral now resembles the basic integral for the inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int\\dfrac{1}{1+u^2}\\,\\textrm d u = \\arctan{u} + C.\n$$\n\nWe make the substitution $u=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt 2}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\sqrt 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14050191/example-472.json" "file_sha256" "6971fcf80e5ddd49db1502806ec3e5d5058537acead60eadae43d95f96e66011"}] "usage" {"q-114027" [] "q-69476" [] "e-470" [] "q-49551" [] "e-5014" [] "q-114030" [] "q-19393" [] "q-49547" [] "e-471" [] "q-114023" [] "q-49505" [] "q-49546" [] "q-19396" [] "q-114056" [] "q-49540" [] "q-73718" [] "e-472" []} "basis" 1747 "retractions" [[17592186064791 :question/problem "What is $∫\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{49 - x^{2}}}dx$?"] [17592186064790 :question/problem "What is $∫\\frac{6}{1 + 9x^{2}}dx$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186063251 17592186063252 17592186063253 17592186063254 17592186063255 1759